{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured locally with `bazel --nohome_rc test --config=embedded",
    "//cmd/bd:bd_embedded_test` -- the exact config bazel.yml's bazel-embedded tier",
    "uses (race, `-test.parallel=4`, tag filter `embedded`), run with the real",
    "committed 20-shard manifest (.github/scripts/embedded-cmd-test-shards.txt)",
    "so every one of the 216 TestEmbedded* functions that existed at capture time",
    "ran exactly once (local sandboxed execution only; no remote executor or",
    "cache flags were configured for this measurement run).",
    "",
    "Each value is that top-level test's own <testcase time=...> from Bazel's",
    "generated test.xml, NOT the enclosing <testsuite time=...>. For this Go test",
    "binary / Bazel version, <testsuite time> was found empirically to be a",
    "wall-clock-since-binary-start timestamp (it does not isolate a concurrently",
    "-run top-level test's own duration under -test.parallel=4 -- e.g. one 308s",
    "test's enclosing testsuite showed 447s because other tests were still in",
    "flight), whereas <testcase time> matched the test binary's own",
    "`--- PASS: TestX (Ys)` line exactly. Do not switch this capture to",
    "<testsuite time> without re-verifying that relationship for the toolchain",
    "in use at the time.",
    "",
    "20 of the originally-measured top-level functions were subsequently split",
    "(same F1 CI-speed pass, see ~/beads-bazel-plan/f1/impl-report.md and bead",
    "bd-f1shard) into 2-3 smaller top-level functions each, to break up single-",
    "test long poles. Those 45 replacement entries are NOT independently",
    "re-measured end-to-end; each is the sum of its assigned subtests' own",
    "<testcase time> from the SAME capture run (every subtest's individual time",
    "was already recorded in that run, since Bazel's XML includes one <testcase>",
    "per `t.Run` leaf) -- i.e., a reconstruction, not a fresh measurement. This",
    "is exact for subtests that ran sequentially within their original parent",
    "(the normal case here; none of these particular subtests call their own",
    "t.Parallel()), and is why some split pieces still land a little over the",
    "180s single-test guideline (e.g. TestEmbeddedInitA at ~197s) -- the split",
    "was grouped for roughly-even subtest *counts*, not for measured duration,",
    "since per-subtest timings were only reconstructed after the split had",
    "already landed. A future --repack after a fresh end-to-end capture could",
    "true these up; not done in this pass given diminishing returns (these are",
    "already far below their pre-split originals of 356-566s).",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is the weighted average seconds-per-init over",
    "every measured test in this file (sum of all durations / sum of all inits,",
    "where inits is discover_inits_cost()'s t.Run( count proxy), used only for a",
    "brand-new test with no entry yet (see",
    "scripts/ci/gen_embedded_cmd_shard_manifest.py's discover_inits_cost()).",
    "",
    "As with the proxied tier's duration file, these are a relative weight for",
    "LPT bin-packing, not an absolute SLA: within-shard -test.parallel=4",
    "overlap, farm noisy-neighbor effects, and future code changes all mean a",
    "shard's total packed cost is a planning estimate, not a guarantee."
  ],
  "seconds_per_init_fallback": 18.0427,
